# Laragon local development

Laragon is the only supported local set-up (see `AGENTS.md` and `docs/local-dev.md`). Never suggest Docker or any other local web stack, and never use `php artisan serve`.

## Live preview gate (before any change)

1. Run `powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts\preview.ps1`. It merges `origin/main` into the current milestone or issue branch (never rebases or pushes), runs `composer install` or `npm ci` when a lock file changed, reports pending migrations (ask before running them), checks Laragon, Apache and MySQL are running, checks `http://apes-newsroom.test/health` serves this checkout's revision through FastCGI, and starts Vite on port 5181.
2. Exit 0: open `http://apes-newsroom.test` in Cursor's browser, confirm it loaded, then say "Preview ready, starting work". Exit 3: a decision is needed, ask with AskQuestion. Exit 1: a blocker, report it.
3. If the site is missing, run `composer setup`. Starting Laragon, clicking Reload, or switching its PHP version needs Bambie's click: ask with AskQuestion.

## Notes

- Agent shells are not Laragon's Terminal: put Laragon's PHP 8.4 and `C:\laragon\bin\nodejs\node-v22` first on `$env:Path` before `composer`, `php artisan` or `npm`.
- Test against the demo data (`composer demo:seed`, `composer demo:reset`; ask before a reset). See `docs/laragon/demo-data.md`.
